abstract: >-
  AnthroSim is a reproducible agent-based simulation framework for deterministic
  demography, resource-constrained permanent household migration,
  evidence-grounded spatial experiments, and explicit temporary mobility and
  aggregation under declared model assumptions. Version 0.3.5 preserves the
  model-semantics-v33 state produced by the complete Scientific Audit v4
  remediation programme. Audit v4 independently interrogated the immutable
  v0.3.4/model-semantics-v25 baseline across Areas A-N, demonstrated 15 findings
  (13 P1 and 2 P2), and all 15 were repaired and independently re-verified or
  dispositioned before closure. The v0.3.5 baseline also incorporates the
  subsequent repository-wide documentation-consistency reconciliation. This
  release is framework-verification/convergence evidence; it does not establish
  empirical archaeological validity or prove model correctness.
